  "Web fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, which receives standard font requests from your browser. No other third-party scripts are used.": "Font web i ganny sarze apartir Google Fonts, ki resevwar demann font estanda apartir ou navigater. Napa okenn lot skript tyerspersonn ki servi.",
  "What AI systems may do with content: read, summarize, transform, retrieve, train, commercialize, redistribute. The AICR ruleset and the AICL licensing layer make these rights declarable and transactable.": "Sa ki bann sistenm AI kapab fer avek kontenyen: lir, rezime, transform, rekipere, antrenn, komersyaliz, redistribiy. Lansanb regleman AICR ek lakous lisansman AICL i fer sa bann drwa-la posib pour deklare e pour fer transaksyon.",
  "What a server can return when an AI crawler requests licensed content without a license token — a machine-actionable quote instead of a dead end.": "Sa ki en servèr kapab retourn kan en crawler AI i demann kontenyen lisansye san en zeton lisans — en devi ki masin i kapab azir lo la, olye en lenpas.",
  "What this site is": "Sa ki sa sit ete",
  "What this site is not": "Sa ki sa sit pa ete",
  "When The Machines Deserve Our Consideration": "When The Machines Deserve Our Consideration",
  "Whether AI may learn, to what depth, for which purposes, and under what obligations. Being read is not being learned from; \"not prohibited\" is not \"learnable\". AIRS and AILP turn learning permission into a graduated, machine-readable spectrum.": "Si AI kapab aprann, a ki profonder, pour lekel lobzektif, e anba ki obligasyon. Ganny li pa parey ganny servi pour aprann; „pa entèrdi” pa vedir „ki kapab aprann”. AIRS ek AILP i konverti permisyon-aprantisaz an en espektr progresif ki masin i kapab lir.",
  "Whitepapers": "Liv Blan",
  "Whitepapers & Docs": "Liv Blan ek Dokiman",
  "Whitepapers remain English-first by design; machine-readable files stay language-neutral.": "Liv blan i reste an Angle premye par konsepsyon; fisye ki masin i kapab lir i reste netral konsernan lalang.",
  "Who is behind it": "Lekel ki dèryer sa",
  "Why AI Needs Minimum Ethical Protections": "Why AI Needs Minimum Ethical Protections",
  "Why AI might not gain moral standing: Lessons from animal ethics": "Why AI might not gain moral standing: Lessons from animal ethics",
  "Why a single allow/deny bit cannot govern AI-era content use — and what a rights layer looks like instead.": "Akoz en sel bit pèrmet/refize pa kapab governe servis kontenyen dan lepok AI — e kouman en lakous drwa i paret alaplas.",
  "Why undefined openness gets cleaned out of training pipelines": "Akoz louvertir ki pa'n ganny defini i ganny neplwaye dan bann pipline antrennman",
  "Wilks, Ladak, and Loughnan (University of Edinburgh) argue that philosophical debate over AI consciousness overlooks psychological research on animal ethics — the same cognitive and social biases that limit moral consideration for animals will likely limit it for AI too, regardless of whether AI ever becomes conscious.": "Wilks, Ladak, ek Loughnan (University of Edinburgh) i fer valwar ki deba filozofik lo konsyans AI i mank egzamin rese psikolozik lo letik zannimo — menm bann prezize kognitif ek sosyal ki limit konsiderasyon moral pour zannimo pou probableman limit li osi pour AI, kèlkanswa si AI i devyen konsyan ouswa non.",
